# upstream PR #1283 (sergqwer): "prefill: bytes_needed sizes the MoE buffers for the layout
# init picks (with or without an expert source)", carried here until it merges.
#
# The prompt path's borrow must match what `carve` (init) allocates.  Upstream #583 (v0.1.39)
# took the first half (the xn / grs count, STRATA_RING_BYTES).  What is left: bytes_needed
# counted the fused layout's smaller MoE buffers for every caller (fused_layout(T, true)),
# while init takes them only when it gets an ExpertSource (fused_layout(T, m.src != nullptr)),
# so a prompt path without one was lent fewer bytes than its unfused buffers take.
# bytes_needed, bytes_needed_no_ring and (0.1.40) bytes_needed_owned - STRATA_OWNED_PRICE=exact's
# sizing - now take the same `src` the callers pass to init.
#
# Measured 2026-10-03 on the ported tree (the whole #547 at the time): borrow 6109 -> 5554 slots
# (11.59 -> 10.51 GiB), prefill -1.77%/-2.59% and pack bytes -2.14%/-1.79% at the 27575 cell
# (128/256 gen), flat at 4344, decode and the cache hit rate unchanged.  Pure accounting: no
# numerics and no configuration.  PR trajectory: #547 -> #1042 (fork mishap) -> #1283 (the
# history rewrite); v0.1.40.2 still does not have it.
#
# Commit e7635b6 (PR #1283's head, rebased onto v0.1.40 by its author), unmodified:
#
